    <string name="gps_off">Off</string>
    <string name="gps_on">On · the watch finds GPS faster</string>
    <string name="gps_needs_server">On · sign in to your server first</string>
    <string name="gps_footer">Your Nimrag server downloads satellite data from Garmin so the watch finds GPS faster; this is Nimrag\'s only contact with Garmin, and the phone only talks to your server.</string>
    <string name="gps_last_title">Last sent to the watch</string>
    <string name="gps_last_never">Not yet</string>
    <string name="gps_last_value">%1$s</string>
    <string name="phone_features_footer">Changing a switch reconnects the watch once, so it learns what the phone can do.</string>
    <string name="phone_notifications_explain">Notifications: your phone\'s notifications appear on the watch, with the title and text, and you can dismiss them from the watch. They go straight to your watch and are never stored or logged by Nimrag.</string>
    <string name="phone_music_explain">Music: the watch shows the song that plays on your phone and its buttons play, pause, skip and change the volume. This needs notification access too, because that is how Android shows the player to an app.</string>
    <string name="phone_find_explain">Find my phone: pressing the find-phone button on the watch makes the phone ring loudly and vibrate, even on silent, until you press \"Found it\", the watch cancels, or the time is up.</string>
    <string name="phone_weather_explain">Weather: your Nimrag server gets the forecast from Open-Meteo for your area, rounded to about 10 km, and sends it to the watch.</string>
    <string name="phone_access_title">Notification access is off</string>
    <string name="phone_access_body">Android keeps a special switch for apps that read notifications. Notifications and music need it. Turn on \"Nimrag Connect\" on the page that opens; nothing is read until a feature is on.</string>
    <string name="phone_access_open">Open the setting</string>
    <string name="phone_access_restricted">If Android says \"App was denied access\" or the switch is greyed out, open the app info, tap the three dots and choose \"Allow restricted settings\" (Android does this for apps installed outside the Play Store), then try again.</string>
    <string name="phone_access_app_info">Open app info</string>
    <string name="phone_access_manage">Notification access</string>
    <string name="phone_access_manage_on">On · tap to change it in system settings</string>
    <string name="phone_fullscreen_note">Android is not letting Nimrag take over the screen, so \"Found it\" appears as a notification you can tap instead.</string>
